 teach."},{"type":"p","text":"They should be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Demonstrate movements"},{"text":"Break complex movements into steps"},{"text":"Count rhythm"},{"text":"Correct posture"},{"text":"Explain expression"},{"text":"Structure rehearsals"},{"text":"Give constructive feedback"},{"text":"Manage different skill levels"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Teaching Process"},{"type":"flow","items":["Demonstrate","Explain","Slow Practice","Group Practice","Individual Correction","Full Sequence","Performance Practice"]}]},{"heading":"Rehearsal Management","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A choreographer is often the leader of the rehearsal room."},{"type":"h","text":"Responsibilities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Set rehearsal schedules"},{"text":"Explain choreography"},{"text":"Manage dancers"},{"text":"Track progress"},{"text":"Correct synchronization"},{"text":"Coordinate music"},{"text":"Coordinate costume requirements"},{"text":"Coordinate technical rehearsals"},{"text":"Prepare performers for stage"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Rehearsal Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Warm-up","Technique","Movement Review","Section Practice","Formation Practice","Full Run","Corrections","Final Run"]}]},{"heading":"Stagecraft","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A choreographer should understand basic:"},{"type":"h","text":"Lighting"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Front lighting"},{"text":"Side lighting"},{"text":"Backlighting"},{"text":"Spotlights"},{"text":"Colour temperature"},{"text":"Transitions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stage"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Entrances"},{"text":"Exits"},{"text":"Wings"},{"text":"Stage depth"},{"text":"Levels"},{"text":"Audience sightlines"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Production"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Costume"},{"text":"Makeup"},{"text":"Props"},{"text":"Set"},{"text":"Projection"},{"text":"Sound"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The choreographer does not need to become a lighting designer, but must understand enough to communicate effectively with the production team."}]},{"heading":"Digital Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Technology is increasingly useful for choreography."},{"type":"h","text":"Essential Tools"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Smartphone video"},{"text":"Video editing"},{"text":"Cloud storage"},{"text":"Presentation software"},{"text":"Canva"},{"text":"Google Drive"},{"text":"Basic project management tools"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Video Editing"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful software:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"DaVinci Resolve"},{"text":"Adobe Premiere Pro"},{"text":"Final Cut Pro"},{"text":"CapCut"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Video can be used to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Review rehearsals"},{"text":"Compare takes"},{"text":"Correct synchronization"},{"text":"Document choreography"},{"text":"Build portfolios"}]}]},{"heading":"AI & Technology in Choreography","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI should be treated as an experimental creative assistant, not as a replacement for artistic judgment or traditional dance knowledge."},{"type":"h","text":"Potential Applications"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Music analysis"},{"text":"Movement documentation"},{"text":"Video organization"},{"text":"Motion analysis"},{"text":"Rehearsal documentation"},{"text":"Concept brainstorming"},{"text":"Visual moodboards"},{"text":"Stage visualization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Motion Capture"},{"type":"p","text":"Emerging motion-capture technologies can record:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Body movement"},{"text":"Position"},{"text":"Timing"},{"text":"Gesture"},{"text":"Spatial trajectories"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Possible workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Dance Performance","Motion Capture","Movement Data","3D Visualization","Movement Analysis","Choreographic Experiment"]}]},{"heading":"Recommended UG Projects","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Original Classical Choreography"},{"type":"p",